spans.s:
Megha,
(1) n. of a previous incarnation of Śākyamuni under Dīpaṃkara, who predicted his enlightenment: Mv 〔i.2.1〕; 〔232.1 ff.〕 (corresponds to Divy Sumati (4), q.v., and to Pali Sumedha, while Pali Megha corresp. to our Meghadatta, q.v.);
(2) n. of another Bodhisattva, a Dravidian (dramiḍa): Gv 〔2.7〕; 〔72.13 ff.〕; Śikṣ 〔36.14〕 (quotation from Gv 〔76.26〕); 〔95.6〕 (allusion to events of Gv 〔73.14 ff.〕).

Meghaśrī,
(1) n. of a monk: Gv 〔2.7〕; 〔58.17〕; 〔59.8 ff.〕;
(2) (˚śiri, m.c.), n. of a Buddha: Gv 〔257.3〕 (vs);
(3) n. of a Bodhisattva: Gv 〔442.5〕.
